From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: Windows 7's minimum part size (TS_MIN)

Purpose: give Windows 7's folder windows their address and search bars at
Windows 7's height.
Windows behavior: on Windows 7, GetThemePartSize(TS_MIN) of an image part
is the sum of its content margins (left + right, top + bottom), at least
1. Measured on Windows 7 for 400 parts of 17 classes (Status, SearchBox,
AddressBand's Navigation, CommandModule, Rebar, Toolbar, Header, ...):
398 follow this; the other 2 are border-fill parts, sized as before.
Wine before: TS_MIN returned the image's size. Explorer sizes its address
and search bands from the search box's minimum size: 23 px tall instead
of 2, which made the bands 47 px tall instead of 26.
Change: with a version 4 (Windows 7) style, TS_MIN of an image part is
the content margins' sum.
Evidence: the folder window's rebar bands are 26 px tall, the toolbar,
tree and list sit at Windows 7's positions (tests/theme-part-sizes.c,
tests/rebar-bands.c).
Scope: version 4 styles; XP styles are unchanged.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/draw.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
index 30d39ba..23a80ac 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/draw.c
@@ -934,6 +934,16 @@ static HRESULT get_image_part_size(HTHEME hTheme, int iPartId, int iStateId, REC
             break;
         }
         case TS_MIN:
+            /* Windows 7 (a version 4 style): the content margins, at least 1
+             * (Explorer sizes its address and search bands from it) */
+            if (MSSTYLES_ActiveThemeFormat4())
+            {
+                MARGINS margins = {0};
+                GetThemeMargins(hTheme, NULL, iPartId, iStateId, TMT_CONTENTMARGINS, NULL, &margins);
+                psz->x = max(1, margins.cxLeftWidth + margins.cxRightWidth);
+                psz->y = max(1, margins.cyTopHeight + margins.cyBottomHeight);
+                break;
+            }
             /* FIXME: couldn't figure how native uxtheme computes min size */
         case TS_TRUE:
             psz->x = rcSrc.right - rcSrc.left;
